Z||000005||StuGood||11-21-2000||07:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RiceBurner515:<BR><B>...a hose that connects to the carb right behind the black connector which is behind the EGR "bell"...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I must confess I'm a little lost!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>Think the one Tigger is talking about is a vinyl tube which runs from a fitting on the aft side of the TB, over to the MAP sensor.  The MAP sensor is mounted on the LHS of the air cleaner housing.<P>The only tube I can think of which runs anywhere near the EGR diaphragm, is the one that actually plugs into the EGR.<P>Hope this helps a little  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">??   <P>||||reg||5
Z||000006||Tigger||11-22-2000||12:24 PM||||Nope, not the one to the MAP sensor.  I'm thinking it might be the tube you have to disconnect from the bottom of the aircleaner to remove it.<P>Yeah, only other one I'm thinking of would go to the EGR valve.||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||11-24-2000||02:25 PM||||Tigger, mine (1988 4-cyl) doesn't seem to have anything like that.  Think the only other lines on mine connect to the vapor canister system (metal lines on aft firewall).<P>Think Tigger's is a 1984 model.  Didn't think the plumbing changed <B>that</B> much, but RiceBurner's is a 1985 SE.  <P>Hopefully, somebody out there can help out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
